       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          TRPTUSE.
       AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
       DATE-WRITTEN.        OCTOBER, 1982.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *C REMARKS.             USAGE REPORT.
      *C
      *C   CI HILLES       NOVEMBER  8, 1983
      *C   UPPED THE FILE LIMIT OF THE S-FILE FOR REPORT FROM 40,000
      *C   TO 50,000 RECORDS.
      *C
      *C   CI HILLES       DECEMBER 13, 1983
      *C   MADE THE FOLLOWING MODIFICATIONS:
      *C     1.  "FULL DESCRIPTION" CAPABILITY ADDED.  IF "FULL DESC"
      *C         OPTION IS PICKED IN "XR10MODE", THIS PGM WILL PRINT
      *C         ALL LINES OF DESCRIPTION FOR EACH CODE.
      *C
      *C     2.  SLIGHT CHANGES TO PRINT FORMAT.  THE CODE HEADING NOW
      *C         PRINTS FOR EACH CODE, RATHER THAN ONLY ONCE AT TOP OF
      *C         PAGE.
      *C
      *C     3.  A PROGRAM ERROR WAS CORRECTED.  IF AN ACCOUNTING
      *C         CLASS WAS SELECTED THAT DID NOT EXIST, SEVERAL "CVAD"
      *C         ERRORS APPEARED IN THE JOB STREAM.
      *C
      *C     4.  IF NO CODES QUALIFIED FOR SELECT OPTION, A MESSAGE
      *C         IS PRINTED ON THE REPORT TO THAT EFFECT.
      *C
      *C   CI HILLES       JUNE 8, 1984
      *C   CHANGED THE "AVG ISS" HEADING
      *C   (STR-MTH-FCST ITEM IN MSTORERM SEGMENT) TO "AVG USE".
      *C   THIS REFLECTS THE CHANGE MADE STARTING JULY 1 - FROM THIS
      *C   TIME ON, THE STR-MTH-FCST FIELD WILL BE UPDATED FROM THE
      *C   USAGE DATA ON THE HP, RATHER THAN TRANSMISSIONS FROM THE
      *C   IBM MAINFRAME.
      *C   NOTE :  THE HEADER FILE FOR THIS REPORT "R10HEAD" WAS
      *C   CHANGED TO REFLECT THE NEW AVERAGE USAGE ALSO.
      *C
      *C   CI HILLES       SEPTEMBER 6, 1984
      *C   CHANGED THE PROGRAM TO USE A SP SPOOLFILE EOF LIMIT OF 60,000
      *C   IF "ALL ITEMS" OPTION IS PICKED (UP FROM 50,000).
      *C
      *C   DA PLUM         MARCH 25, 1984
      *C   MADE THE FOLLOWING PROGRAM CHANGES:
      *C     1) THE REPORT OPTIONS WILL NOW BE COBOL "ACCEPT"ED FROM
      *C        PROGRAM "TRSCREEN" RATHER THAN READ IN FROM A FILE.
      *C        PROGRAM "XR10MODE" IS NO LONGER IN USE.
      *C     2) ADDED AN ACCEPT OF ROUTING DATA WHICH IS PROVIDED BY
      *C        "TRSCREEN" AND A CALL TO "THDPRT2" WHICH USES THIS DATA
      *C        TO PRINT A HEADER PAGE.
      *C     3) THE REPORT OPTIONS WERE REVISED TO ALLOW THE SELECTION
      *C        OF A RANGE OF CORPORATE CODES OR ACCOUNTING CLASSES,
      *C        RATHER THAN HAVING THE USER SELECT A FIXED NUMBER OF
      *C        MAJOR GROUPS OR ACCOUNTING CLASSES.
      *C     4) THE REPORT HEADING WAS REVISED TO IDENTIFY THE SORT AND
      *C        MATERIAL OPTIONS CHOOSEN, INCLUDING THE RANGE SPECIFIED.
      *C     5) SUBPROGRAM "TDATECHK" WAS INCORPORATED WHICH SOLVES THE
      *C        PROBLEM OF EUROPEAN DATES.  THIS SUBPROGRAM RETURNS THE
      *C        DATE IN THE PROPER FORMAT FOR EACH PLANT.
      *C
      *C   DA PLUM         JULY 30, 1985
      *C   CHANGED TEXT LENGTH TO 55 FOR ALL TYPES OF
      *C   PRINTERS REGARDLESS OF THE REPORT OPTIONS CHOOSEN.
      *C
      *C   CJ ROBINSON     JANUARY 20, 1987
      *C   CHANGED TO CALL SUBPROGRAM "CDESC" TO GET FULL DESCRIPTION
      *C   IF REQUESTED.
      *C
      *C   CR KALMAN       DECEMBER 1, 1993
      *C   WHEN THIS PROGRAM WAS CONVERTED TO THE AS/400 THE SCREEN
      *C   SHOWING THE POSSIBLE SELECTIONS NO LONGER REQUIRES THE
      *C   SORT OPTION TO BE ENTERED. IF LEFT EMPTY, THIS CAUSES THE
      *C   PROGRAM TO BLOWUP. SINCE THERE IS NO EASY WAY TO FORCE THIS
      *C   OPTION TO BE REQUIRED, I AM DEFAULTING THE SORT OPTION TO "1"
      *C   IF IT IS LEFT BLANK. THIS CAN BE CHANGED TO ANOTHER OPTION
      *C   IF IT'S BETTER.  ALSO ADDED THE COMMENT "(DEFAULT = 1)" TO
      *C   THE DSPF ZRSCREEN, RECORD FR10SCRN.
      *C  JUNE 23, 1994   CR KALMAN
      *C   ADDED CALL TO COBOL ERROR HANDLER -MCXCBLERR.
      *C
      *C  SEPT 03, 1996   CA YODER
      *C     MODIFIED PROGRAM FOR CENTURY DATABASE CHANGES.
      *C
      *C  07/24/1997   CA YODER     REQ #95-015
      *C    MODIFIED PROGRAM TO ACCEPT AND USE THE NEW OPTIONS ADDED
      *C    TO THE MATERIALS CONTROL REPORTS.
      *C    NOTE:  THIS PROGRAM NOW USES COPYLIB MEMBERS FOR MOST OF
      *C           ITS PROCESSING LOGIC.  TO SEE ALL OF THE MEMBERS,
      *C           LOOK IN COPYLIB FOR THE FILES THAT START WITH THE
      *C           PREFIX "MTLS".
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C
      *C  01/28/98    CA YODER
      *C     TOOK OUT PAGE ADVANCE BETWEEN CONTROL BREAKS FOR KEYWORD/
      *C     MODIFIER SORT.  USERS COMPLAINED THAT THE REPORT IS TOO
      *C     LONG WITH ALL THE PAGE BREAKS.
      *C

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       SPECIAL-NAMES. C01 IS NEWPAGE.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT SORT-FILE     ASSIGN TO DISK-SORT.
           SELECT ONLINE-PRT ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.
           SELECT MPLTINFO-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DDESC-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1401
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT USAGEFIL-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCSUSAG
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DMANPART-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS3603
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.

       COPY MTLSSORT IN COPYLIB.

      *SD  SORT-FILE
      *    RECORD CONTAINS 242 CHARACTERS.
      *01  SORT-RCD.
      *    05  SORT-DETAIL.
      *        10  SORT-CODE          PIC X(8).
      *        10  SORT-CLASS         PIC X(4).
      *        10  SORT-UM            PIC XX.
      *        10  SORT-ONHAND        PIC S9(8).
      *        10  SORT-MTH-FCST      PIC S9(8).
      *        10  SORT-YTD-USAGE     PIC S9(8).
      *        10  SORT-USAGES OCCURS 14 TIMES.
      *            15  SORT-USAGE     PIC S9(8).
      *        10  SORT-PRIM-LOC      PIC X(12).
      *        10  SORT-DESC          PIC X(80).

       FD  ONLINE-PRT
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
           RECORD CONTAINS 132 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS PRINT-RCD.
       01  PRINT-RCD.
           05  PRINT-LINE           PIC X(132).

       FD  MPLTINFO-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       FD  MSTORERM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  DDESC-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DDESC-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1400  OF MCFLCS1401.

       FD  USAGEFIL-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  USAGEFIL-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCSUSAG  OF MCFLCSUSAG.

       FD  DMANPART-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DMANPART-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS3600  OF MCFLCS3603.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       77  PLT-ARG                    PIC X(4)   VALUE "P 01".
      *----------  CODE-CTR :  NUMBER OF CODES PRINTED ON REPORT
       77  CODE-CTR                   PIC 9(5)   VALUE 0.
       77  PAGE-CTR                   PIC S9(4)  COMP       VALUE 0.
       77  LINE-ADV                   PIC S9(4)  COMP       VALUE 0.
       77  FILE-IS-RETURNED           PIC X      VALUE "N".
       77  YEAR-TO-DATE               PIC S9(9)  COMP-4.
       77  TOTAL-ONHAND               PIC S9(9)  VALUE 0.
       77  TOTAL-MTD-USAGE            PIC S9(9)  VALUE 0.
       77  TOTAL-YTD-USAGE            PIC S9(9)  VALUE 0.
       77  SUB                        PIC S9(4)  COMP-4.
       77  SUB2                       PIC S9(4)  COMP-4.
       77  SUB3                       PIC S9(4)  COMP-4.
       77  MM-9                       PIC 99.
       77  PREV-MONTH                 PIC 99.
       77  SAVE-CLASS                 PIC X(4).
      *---------- CODES-RELEASED:  NUMBER OF CODES RELEASED TO PRINT ROUTINES
      *77  CODES-RELEASED             PIC 9(5)   VALUE 0.
       77  TEXT-LEFT                  PIC 9(2)   VALUE 0.
       77  TEXT-LENGTH                PIC 9(2)   VALUE 55.
       77  TEXT-TO-PRINT              PIC 9(2)   VALUE 0.
       77  LINE-CTR                   PIC 9(2)   VALUE 1.
      *------------ CODES-STR-TOTAL:  TOTAL NUMBER OF CODES IN STOREROOM
      *------------ DEFINED AS CODES WHOSE REORDER POINT > 0
       77  CODES-STR-TOTAL            PIC 9(5)   VALUE 0.

9406CK 01  SCOPE   PIC X.

      *-------- ACCOUNT FOR CENTURY.
       01  DATE-BUFFER-CN.
           05  CC-BUF                 PIC 99.
           05  DATE-BUFFER.
               10  YY-BUF             PIC 99.
               10  MM-BUF             PIC 99.
               10  DD-BUF             PIC 99.

       01  DATE-BUFFER-R   REDEFINES  DATE-BUFFER-CN.
           05  R-YEAR                 PIC 9(4).
           05  FILLER                 PIC 9(4).

       01  YEAR-AGO-DATE-CN.
           05  YEAR-AGO-YYYY          PIC 9(4).
           05  YEAR-AGO-MM            PIC 99.
           05  YEAR-AGO-DD            PIC 99.

      ****** PARMS FOR CALL TO "THDPRT2" (HEADER PAGE SUBPROG)  ******
      ****** HD-ROUTE-DATA IS ACCEPTED FROM PGM "TRSCREEN".    ******

       01  HD-RET-CODE                PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       01  HD-FILE-NAME               PIC X(17) VALUE SPACES.
       01  FNUM                       PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.

       COPY OVRPFDATA IN COPYLIB.
       COPY CCHKOBJ IN COPYLIB.

       01  SAVE-DESC-AREA.
           05  SAVE-DESC-LINE OCCURS 15 TIMES.
               10  SAVE-DESC          PIC X(80).

       COPY TCHKBLKT IN COPYLIB.

       COPY MTLSWORK IN COPYLIB.

      *---------- USAGE INFO.
       01  HOLD-YTD-USAGE     PIC S9(8).
       01  USAGE-TABLE.
           05  HOLD-USAGES OCCURS 14 TIMES.
               10  HOLD-USAGE     PIC S9(8).

       01  SWITCH-AREA.
           05  END-OF-INPUT-FILE               PIC X VALUE "N".
               88  ALL-INPUT-RECORDS-PROCESSED       VALUE "Y".

